      "review": "The norm of exp(-c) is less than one for c>0. For n=0 or n>=1, n<=n^2; multiplication by -c reverses the inequality. Thus exp(-c*n^2)<=exp(-c*n)=exp(-c)^n. The complete real norm comparison and geometric summability theorem give Summable.",
